The A-series (A0, A1, A2, A3, A4…) is defined(?) by ISO 216 and has an aspect ratio of √2.
-
The size of A0 is is 1 m².

The B-series also has an aspect ratio of √2.
-
The size of a B sized paper is the geometric mean of the larger and smaller A sized paper.
-
B0 has an area of √2 m² with a width of 1 meter.

The C-series is (was?) the international standard for letters.
-
The size of Cn is the geometric mean of An and Bn.

ISO 216 originated from DIN 476.

North american paper sizes include
  • Letter
  • Legal
  • Ledger


